ents are true.\n\n- $(x,y)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(x,2)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(1,y)\\in A\\times B$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times B,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B$ at each intersection.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/c33000e8aa6c217b5607e43e961aaea10586b615d633dc1b59cc598e2f7af56c.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(x,y)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\n- $(x,2)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\n- $(1,y)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-181279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e9