, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-1261" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1261" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1261" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the sets $A={2,4,6},$ $B={x,y},$ and $C=A\\times B,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(2,4)\\in C$\n- $(2,x)\\in C$\n- $(3,y)\\in C$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $A\\times B$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/df4277feac4c4e838538f941aa0a07d087beb9005d8f7a8347dadc1da7fe975e.png)\n\nHence, the set $C=A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nC={(2,x),(2,y),(4,x),(4,y),(6,x),(6,y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-1257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the sets $X={f,g,h}$ and $Z=X\\times X,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(f,g)\\in Z$\n- $(f,g,h)\\in Z$\n- $(h,h)\\in Z$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $X\\times X$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $X.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${X}^{2}=X\\times X$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/1718bd6f3f2eaa8dd8fe581b0d938b3b5f1928d5e56a11a324f145e7a481fabe.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times X$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(f,f),(f,g),(f,h),(g,f),(g,g),(g,h),(h,f),(h,g),(h,h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/