ic for ${X}^{2}=X\\times X$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/e7c24108e0d9f5e2e7edbfbe90cdf7318bc247aa73a4c9c72dc61449c7b4da94.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times X$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(k,k),(k,m),(k,n),(m,k),(m,m),(m,n),(n,k),(n,m),(n,n)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-182021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the sets $X={5,10},$ $Y={r,s,t},$ and $Z=X\\times Y,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(5,r)\\in Z$\n- $(r,t)\\in Z$\n- $(10,s)\\in Z$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $X\\times Y$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/1eb13d93fbefc4c7285edef537a9fb3e21339f7a3b37a179eeb150db8d726c1b.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(5,r),(5,s),(5,t),(10,r),(10,s),(10,t)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-182015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-182015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the cardinality of $C\\times D$ for $C={0,1,2,...,11}$ and $D={s,t,u,v}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For any two finite sets $C$ and $D,$ the cardinality of $C\\times D$ is\n\n$$\n|C\\times D|=|C|\\cdot |D|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|C\\times D| & =|C|\\cdot |D| \\\\  & =12\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-80896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "40"] ["math" "48"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "48"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-105865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the cardinality of $K\\times K$ for $K={k,l,m,n,o,p,r,s}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-105865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For any two finite sets $A$ and $B,$ the cardinality of $A\\times B$ is\n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|K\\times K| & =|K|\\cdot |K| \\\\  & =8\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-captur