ny two finite sets $A$ and $B,$ the cardinality of $A\\times B$ is\n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A\\times B| & =|A|\\cdot |B| \\\\  & =8\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-80442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "28"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "40"] ["math" "45"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the cardinality of $H\\times K$ for $H={1,2,3,…,9}$ and $K={x,y}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For any two finite sets $H$ and $K,$ the cardinality of $H\\times K$ is\n\n$$\n|H\\times K|=|H|\\cdot |K|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|H\\times K| & =|H|\\cdot |K| \\\\  & =9\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-80894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-80894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the cardinality of $Z\\times Y$ for $Z={1,4,9,16,25,36}$ and $Y={2,3,7,9}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For any two finite sets $Z$ and $Y,$ the cardinality of $Z\\times Y$ is\n\n$$\n|Z\\times Y|=|Z|\\cdot |Y|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|Z\\times Y| & =|Z|\\cdot |Y| \\\\  & =6\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-1264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-1264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A={-1,1}$ and $B={u,v},$ which of the following elements belong to $B\\times B\\times A?$\n\n- $(v,v,1)$\n- $((v,v),1)$\n- $(1,v,u)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $A\\times B\\times C$ consists of all ordered triples whose first coordinate belongs to $A,$ second coordinate belongs to $B,$ and third coordinate belongs to $C.$\n\nIn this case, $B\\times B\\times A$ consists of every combination of ${u,v}$ with ${u,v}$ and ${-1,1},$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\times B\\times A={ & (u,u,-1),(u,u,1),(u,v,-1),(u,v,1), \\\\  & (v,u,-1),(v,u,1),(v,v,-1),(v,v,1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n|B\\times B\\times A|=|B|\\cdot |B|\\cdot |A|=2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $(v,v,1)\\in B\\times B\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-181295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A={0,1,2}$ and $B={x,y},$ which of the following elements belong to $(A\\times B)\\times A?$\n\n- $(1,y,2)$\n- $((1,y),2)$\n- $((y,1),y)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${0,1,2}$ with ${x,y},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/077da578323a686ecf0e07cf0a56030fa4ce128a74d408af95b8a3027ad13f28.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(0,x),(0,y),(1,x),(1,y),(2,x),(2,y)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|=3\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(A\\times B)\\times A\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A\\times B$ and $A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/3a14abffc755dcfccce2d410ea18fbcae42d4afe2fbeffd81e1a291bc9d4968e.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(A\\times B)\\times A|=|A\\times B|\\cdot |A|=6\\cdot 3=18.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $((1,y),2)\\in (A\\times B)\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-181294" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181294" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181294" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A={v,w}$ and $B={3,4,5},$ which of the following elements belong to $A\\times B\\times A?$\n\n- $(v,4,5)$\n- $(v,3,w)$\n- $(w,5,w)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $A\\times B\\times C$ consists of all ordered triples whose first coordinate belongs to $A,$ second coordinate belongs to $B,$ and the third coordinate belongs to $C.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B\\times A$ consists of every combination of ${v,w}$ with ${3,4,5}$ and ${v,w},$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\times B\\times A={ & (v,3,v),(v,3,w),(v,4,v),(v,4,w),(v,5,v),(v,5,w), \\\\  & (w,3,v),(w,3,w),(w,4,v),(w,4,w),(w,5,v),(w,5,w)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n|A\\times B\\times A|=|A|\\cdot |B|\\cdot |A|=2\\cdot 3\\cdot 2=12.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $(v,3,w)$ and $(w,5,w)$ are in $A\\times B\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-181945" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181945" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181945" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A={4,8}$ and $B={x,y,z},$ which of the following elements belong to $A\\times (A\\times B)?$\n\n- $(4,(8,z))$\n- $(8,(8,x))$\n- $(8,4,y)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${4,8}$ with ${x,y,z},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/72feee192b949dcce7b0f10f4e1d772c809bcf73de6c66f15c7de75a4a1ff672.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(4,x),(4,y),(4,z),(8,x),(8,y),(8,z)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times (A\\times B)\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A$ and $A\\times B,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/1ae41857d4aee82a2a4ad838c20bbe72b05a1505a5f4df3aa4a86fda0fff0612.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times (A\\times B)|=|A|\\cdot |A\\times B|=2\\cdot 6=12.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $(4,(8,z))$ and $(8,(8,x))$ are in $A\\times \\text{\\(}A\\times B).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-181977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A={p,q,r}$ and $B={3,5},$ which of the following elements belong to $B\\times (A\\times A)?$\n\n- $(5,(r,p))$\n- $(q,(5,3))$\n- $(3,q,p)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times A$ consists of every combination of ${p,q,r}$ with ${p,q,r},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/aad91ef7655fa8a5bf0c9852ee4e5e2166289087a56ac18e932ee3cce17164a0.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times A={(p,p),(p,q),(p,r),(q,p),(q,q),(q,r),(r,p),(r,q),(r,r)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times A|=|A|\\cdot |A|=3\\cdot 3=9.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nB\\times (A\\times A)\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $B$ and $A\\times A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/e573cecaa9333e071d980b1b03d65dafadd027506d2c2b9b6e8acfbe15d3be52.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|B\\times (A\\times A)|=|B|\\cdot |A\\times A|=2\\cdot 9=18.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $(5,(r,p))\\in B\\times (A\\times A).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44a9f5f87dfc93935f604664377abdb446e1f5a533f69f4c9d7e207150b5d657"} {"question" "q-181969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "q-181969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/state.json" "file_sha256" "51ca0549cbc0f4fd94f09e93c734d27673a55c16efd3051935448cb23db2d5e1"} {"question" "e-13160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Construct a schematic of the set $A^2$ for $A = \\{0,3 \\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/example-13160.json" "file_sha256" "a8c8462cb648875705d2dc06d0b6945b08f94ccbc3448a76baef30fa4d817c31"} {"question" "e-13160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $A^2$ is equivalent to the Cartesian product $A^2 = A \\times A.$\n\nThe Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo create a schematic of the Cartesian product $A\\times A$, we create a table and list the elements of the first set $A$ in a row across the top and the elements of the second set $A$ in a column down the left side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/4646235c2009dc45d7d09a52162ec0bdf929d122f450791ae9917b3ad8ef5a43.png)\n\nThen, at each intersection, we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of the first set and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of the second set.\n\nOur completed $A \\times A$ schematic is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/8c9647361885913d2534fefb49a878c2e365cf5be36d1bb4c059d95344dd1a60.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/example-13160.json" "file_sha256" "a8c8462cb648875705d2dc06d0b6945b08f94ccbc3448a76baef30fa4d817c31"} {"question" "e-13151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the sets $A = \\{3,4,7\\},$ $B = \\{f,g\\},$ and $C = A \\times B,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(f,4) \\in C$\n\n- $(7,g) \\in C$\n\n- $(3,f) \\in C$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/example-13151.json" "file_sha256" "11908d28785e51baba7b1e8379148dc62af3adb8d2909e120d673cd442bbac67"} {"question" "e-13151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $A \\times B$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/683bad9c822cea7218b2fd8a252e46215103c95b3ee9c42e41e7141ed8a40330.png)\n\nHence, the set $C = A \\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nC = \\big\\{ \\bbox[2pt, Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}(3,f)}, (3, g), (4, f), (4, g), (7, f), \\bbox[2pt, Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}(7,g)}\\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/example-13151.json" "file_sha256" "11908d28785e51baba7b1e8379148dc62af3adb8d2909e120d673cd442bbac67"} {"question" "e-13154" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $C = \\{ 3, 4, 7, 9, 11 \\}$ and $D  =\\{ 1, 2, 3, \\ldots, 10 \\},$ what is the cardinality of $C \\times D?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/example-13154.json" "file_sha256" "ee1eaea891c69fddc586c269acbcd4b2633f118b5f03d5f1f59d85152ca0ba22"} {"question" "e-13154" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For any two finite sets $C$ and $D,$ the cardinality of $C \\times D$ is\n\n$$\n| C \\times D | = |C| \\cdot |D|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|C\\times D| & =|C|\\cdot |D| \\\\  & =5\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/example-13154.json" "file_sha256" "ee1eaea891c69fddc586c269acbcd4b2633f118b5f03d5f1f59d85152ca0ba22"} {"question" "e-13152" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A = \\{ p,q \\}$ and $B = \\{ 4,9 \\},$ which of the following elements belong to $(A \\times B) \\times B?$\n\n- $((p,4),9)$\n\n- $((q,9),4)$\n\n- $(p,4,9)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/example-13152.json" "file_sha256" "5f5fb79636b1e812fb7fe02cf2c93b67f4d6cc3d424b4bf22b3806c67459e738"} {"question" "e-13152" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A \\times B$ consists of every combination of $\\{ p,q \\}$ with $\\{ 4,9 \\},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/69ff8391a11b7bfa221b6b303f31551288bd969bdeed778fb05d3b7094e027ae.png)\n\nHence, the set $A \\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA \\times B = \\{ (p,4), (p,9), (q,4), (q,9)\\}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A \\times B| = |A| \\cdot |B| = 2 \\cdot 2 = 4.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(A \\times B) \\times B\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A \\times B$ and $B,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/5f4a74a98f9df15273d59131eadc1155ff2d1105e1027e7d10b7e2366102e046.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(A \\times B) \\times B| = |A \\times B| \\cdot |B| = 4 \\cdot 2 = 8.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}((p, 4), 9)}$ and $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}((q,9),4)}$ are in $(A \\times B) \\times B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/example-13152.json" "file_sha256" "5f5fb79636b1e812fb7fe02cf2c93b67f4d6cc3d424b4bf22b3806c67459e738"}] "usage" {"q-1257" [] "q-181295" [] "e-13154" [] "e-13152" [] "q-1264" [] "e-13151" [] "q-181287" [] "q-181294" [] "e-13160" []} "basis" 1433 "retractions" [[17592186054982 :question/problem "Which of the following is a schematic of the Cartesian product $A \\cdot B$ for $A = {1, 10, 100}$ and $B = {a, b}$?"] [17592186054906 :question/problem "For the sets $A = {2, 4, 6}$, $B = {x, y}$, and $C = A \\cdot B$, determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n1. $(2, 4) ∈ C$\n2. $(2, x) ∈ C$\n3. $(3, y) ∈ C$"] [17592186054909 :question/problem "What is the cardinality of $Z \\cdot Y$ for $Z = {1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36}$ and $Y = {2, 3, 7, 9}$?"] [17592186054985 :question/problem "If $A = {-1, 1}$ and $B = {u, v}$, which of the following elements belong to $B \\cdot B \\cdot A$?\n\n1. $(v, v, 1)$\n2. $((v, v), 1)$\n3. $(1, v, u)$"] [17592186054984 :question/problem "If $A = {0, 1, 2}$ and $B = {x, y}$, which of the following elements belong to $(A \\cdot B) \\cdot A$?\n\n1. $(1, y, 2)$\n2. $((1, y), 2)$\n3. $((y, 1), y)$"] [17592186054351 :question/problem "Construct a schematic of the set $A^2$ for $A = \\{0,3 \\}$."] [17592186054351 :question/worked-solution "The set $A^2$ is equivalent to the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA^2 = A \\times A\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B$.\n\nTo create a schematic of the Cartesian product $A\\times A$, we create a table and list the elements of the first set $A$ in a row across the top and the elements of the second set $A$ in a column down the left side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/49/Source/Images/144ff19e358a073bcea04a9719793455.png)\n\nThen, at each intersection, we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of the first set and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of the second set.\n\nOur completed $A \\times A$ schematic is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/49/Source/Images/4f01eda6f1609be0d129be13ac2d565c.png)"] [17592186054348 :question/problem "For the sets $A = \\{3,4,7\\}$, $B = \\{f,g\\}$, and $C = A \\times B$, determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n1. $(f,4) \\in C$\n2. $(7,g) \\in C$\n3. $(3,f) \\in C$"] [17592186054348 :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B$.\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $A \\times B$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/49/Source/Images/488cc12c3ff8d8b797a5ecd57846bd45.png)\n\nHence, the set\n\n$$\nC = A \\times B\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\nC = \\big\\{\\bbox[2pt, Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}(3,f)}, (3, g), (4, f), (4, g), (7, f), \\bbox[2pt, Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}(7,g)}\\big\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""] [17592186054350 :question/problem "If $C = \\{3, 4, 7, 9, 11 \\}$ and $D =\\{1, 2, 3, \\ldots, 10 \\}$, what is the cardinality of $C \\times D$?"] [17592186054350 :question/worked-solution "For any two finite sets $C$ and $D$, the cardinality of $C \\times D$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}C \\times D & = & C & \\cdot & D\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}C \\cdot D & &= & C & \\cdot & D\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 5 \\cdot 10 \\\\\n&= 50\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186054349 :question/problem "If $A = \\{p,q \\}$ and $B = \\{4,9 \\}$, which of the following elements belong to $(A \\times B) \\times B$?\n\n1. $((p,4),9)$\n2. $((q,9),4)$\n3. $(p,4,9)$"] [17592186054349 :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B$.\n\nIn this case, $A \\times B$ consists of every combination of $\\{p,q \\}$ with $\\{4,9 \\}$, as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/49/Source/Images/41f76e800a83fdbf548fb4a281d338f4.png)\n\nHence, the set $A \\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA \\times B = \\{(p,4), (p,9), (q,4), (q,9)\\}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}A \\times B & = & A & \\cdot & B\\end{vmatrix} = 2 \\cdot 2 = 4\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n$(A \\times B) \\times B$\nconsists of every combination of $A \\times B$ and $B$, as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/49/Source/Images/12cd1413549bdde65ed735cf3e17b99f.png)\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}(A \\times B) \\times B & = & A \\times B & \\cdot & B\\end{vmatrix} = 4 \\cdot 2 = 8\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}((p, 4), 9)}$ and $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}((q,9),4)}$ are in $(A \\times B) \\times B$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""]] "immutable_answers" [17592186051402 17592186051403 17592186051404 17592186051405 17592186051406 17592186051420 17592186051421 17592186051422 17592186051423 17592186051424 17592186051816 17592186051817 17592186051818 17592186051819 17592186051820 17592186051828 17592186051829 